      {
        "id": 93291,
        "name": "Silverleaf",
        "username": "Silverleaf",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/{size}/2332_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-23T14:16:42.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Turret Mode means Bunker can't draw cards, even out of turn. He could use Initialise, but it wouldn't allow him to draw a card. Ammo Drop is an exception since you can draw from its effect even if a Mode says you can't draw.</p><p>Stuff like this is carefully worded - contrast with Unity's Bots which say they cannot be played&nbsp;<em>during Unity's play phase.</em>&nbsp;This means they CAN be played at any other time, if someone lets Unity play out of turn for example. If Modes were meant to prevent only playing/drawing/power use during that part of Bunker's turn they'd be worded in the same way - such as \"Bunker may not draw cards during his draw phase\".</p><p>Similarly, an effect that says heroes can't use powers, means heroes can't use powers&nbsp;<em>period.</em></p><p>Oh and welcome! If you have a microphone and a G+ account you're most welcome to join in the regular games some of us play over there, if you're tired of solo play!</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:19:28.633Z",
