        "raw": "<p>Turret Mode means Bunker can&#39;t draw cards, even out of turn. He could use Initialise, but it wouldn&#39;t allow him to draw a card. Ammo Drop is an exception since you can draw from its effect even if a Mode says you can&#39;t draw.</p><p>Stuff like this is carefully worded - contrast with Unity&#39;s Bots which say they cannot be played&nbsp;<em>during Unity&#39;s play phase.</em>&nbsp;This means they CAN be played at any other time, if someone lets Unity play out of turn for example. If Modes were meant to prevent only playing/drawing/power use during that part of Bunker&#39;s turn they&#39;d be worded in the same way - such as &quot;Bunker may not draw cards during his draw phase&quot;.</p><p>Similarly, an effect that says heroes can&#39;t use powers, means heroes can&#39;t use powers&nbsp;<em>period.</em></p><p>Oh and welcome! If you have a microphone and a G+ account you&#39;re most welcome to join in the regular games some of us play over there, if you&#39;re tired of solo play!</p>",
